========================================================================
fdlibm (via V8)
========================================================================

jsfdlibm.go contains Go ports of the fdlibm e_pow.c and e_log.c routines
as vendored and used by V8 (v8/src/base/ieee754.cc, BSD-3-Clause
license). These are the exact routines JavaScript's Math.pow and Math.log
execute on V8, ported so scores match fuse.js bit-for-bit. The original
fdlibm notice:

    Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved.

    Developed at SunSoft, a Sun Microsystems, Inc. business.
    Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this
    software is freely granted, provided that this notice
    is preserved.

V8 itself is licensed under BSD-3-Clause:
https://github.com/v8/v8/blob/main/LICENSE

========================================================================
Unicode tables
========================================================================

unicode_tables.go is generated data, produced by running Node.js (V8)
over every Unicode code point: String.prototype.toLowerCase behavior and
the NFD + combining-mark normalization that fuse.js's stripDiacritics
performs. It contains no upstream source code. The underlying character
data derives from the Unicode Character Database, whose license is at
https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
